5. Verification and Troubleshooting
•	Address plan: PC0 `192.168.1.10/24`, Router0 LAN `192.168.1.1`, transit `10.0.0.1/30`; Router1 transit `10.0.0.2/30`, LAN `192.168.2.1`, PC1 `192.168.2.10/24`.
•	If ping fails, check cable/link lights, interface IPs, `no shutdown`, default gateways, static routes, matching pre-shared keys, mirrored ACLs and peer addresses.
•	Packet Tracer device models/IOS images differ; if a command is unsupported, use a compatible router image or follow the supported equivalent shown by your course environment.
6. Expected Result
A site-to-site IPsec configuration is applied between the two routers, and LAN-to-LAN connectivity and IPsec counters are checked.
7. Shortcut / Improvement Notes
Configure and verify basic routing before adding IPsec. This separates routing problems from VPN negotiation problems.
8. Conclusion
A site-to-site IPsec configuration is applied between the two routers, and LAN-to-LAN connectivity and IPsec counters are checked.
